Copyright 2026 Yuriy Orlov <yuriy.orlov@undertrust.dev>

This product includes software originally developed and first published
by Yuriy Orlov in September 2026 at https://github.com/yurgeno/saut.

SAUT implements cross-harness assurance for agent skills: one skill source
is judged against a capability registry that records, per harness, what a
declared tool allowlist actually means there — a restriction, a
pre-approval grant, informational prose, or a field dropped on render —
and that recorded semantics is then measured by executing the skill in
each harness and comparing observed tool calls against the declaration.
This design and its terminology were conceived and first published by
Yuriy Orlov.

